index 3ab8a19..5fca173 100644
--- a/docs/security_analysis.md
+++ b/docs/security_analysis.md
@@ -417,3 +417,113 @@ All six eFuse key blocks (KEY0-KEY5) are allocated by this plan. Zero spare.
 The recommendation is to keep one SBV2 rotation slot in reserve rather than
 filling all three.
 
+
+---
+
+## 7. Phase 19 appendix — runtime remanence & glitch hardening (reversible)
+
+All items below are reversible (flash writes only, virtual eFuses).
+No `espefuse.py` / `idf.py efuse` action. Headless proofs over UART.
+
+### G1. Panic/WDT/shutdown scrub (test payload `test_payloads/canary_scrub`)
+
+After the JMP handoff the loader is gone, so payload runtime secrets can
+only be scrubbed inside the crashing payload. The test payload registers
+both `esp_register_shutdown_handler(scrub_fn)` (covers `esp_restart()`) and
+a `--wrap=esp_restart_noos` interceptor (covers `abort()`/panic/task-WDT,
+which bypass shutdown handlers on IDF v5.5). `scrub_fn` is ROM-safe:
+volatile word writes over the fixed canary window + barrier, no
+malloc/free, no FATFS, no float printf. Scrub window is bounded (1 KB
+canary; secret window 1 MB design target, <200 ms budget). HP_SYS_WDT
+hardware resets may bypass both hooks — recorded per reset source, kept as
+a known limitation.
+
+### G2. Warm-reset canary proof
+
+Fixed canary (`CANARY_PADDR`/`CANARY_LEN` in `loader_config.h`, per-target;
+sign-time overlap check in `tools/check_canary_overlap.py`). The loader
+inspector runs before any SD/PSRAM alloc, gated on warm reset reasons +
+`RTC_TEST_MAGIC` at the fixed RTC word, compares with a volatile word loop
+(no `memcmp`), logs `CANARY_REMANENT` vs `CANARY_CLEARED`, zeroes its read
+buffer, and clears the magic. Campaign: `scrub_off`+plant+fault →
+`REMANENT` (control), then `scrub_on`+plant+fault → `CLEARED` (patched).
+pytest gate: `--canary` (see `conftest.py`; default off so normal CI with
+the MicroPython payload is unaffected).
+
+### G3. Verify-path glitch hardening
+
+Every loader gate converts to `SECURE_OK 0x5A5A` / `SECURE_FAIL 0xA5A5`
+(Hamming distance 16) immediately and is double-branched with a compiler
+barrier between checks (`secure_check_double()` in `bundle_validate.h`;
+disassembly must show two compares — `volatile` + barrier prevent folding).
+No crypto re-run (would cost seconds per boot); only the decision is
+redundant. Bounded 1–5 ms `esp_fill_random` jitter before multisig on every
+boot (no oracle), logged as `jitter_ms`. Host-locked in
+`host_test/tests/test_secure_status.cpp` (magic distance, strictness,
+simulated single-skip fails closed).
+
+### G4. memzero coverage audit
+
+Every `halt` path runs `halt_and_scrub()` (`psram_buf` + `image_plan_t` +
+inspector buffer) with the barrier-safe volatile loop, never `memset`.
+`esp_image.c` fatal paths scrub `fake_flash` + plan before halting.
+Catch2 regression: corrupt/truncated bundles map to `SECURE_FAIL`; no early
+return without scrub by construction.
+
+### G1/G2 silicon proof (ESP32-P4 v1.3, Oct 16 2026 — PASS)
+
+Canary payload `test_payloads/canary_scrub` (192 KB, signed `--version 1`,
+overlap-checked) driven over UART; loader flashed with `CONFIG_SPIRAM_MEMTEST=n`:
+
+```
+# Boot A — control (scrub_off + plant + fault_restart)
+> CANARY_PLANTED addr=0x48400000 len=1024 pattern=0xCA4A5EED
+rst:0xc (SW_CPU_RESET)
+I SEEDSIGNER_LOADER: INSPECT Canary 0x48400000: CANARY_REMANENT
+  (non-zero words=256 first at +0x0 first_word=0xCA4A5EED)
+
+# Boot B — patched (scrub_on + plant + fault_restart)
+I SEEDSIGNER_LOADER: INSPECT Canary 0x48400000: CANARY_CLEARED (1024/1024 zero)
+```
+
+`first_word=0xCA4A5EED` matches the planted pattern exactly, proving
+loader/payload PSRAM-view agreement. Repeated for `fault_abort` (panic →
+`--wrap=esp_restart_noos`) and `fault_wdt` (INT-WDT spin → panic → wrapper):
+both `CANARY_CLEARED`. HP_SYS_WDT hardware reset remains uncovered by design
+(no software runs) — documented limitation, same as §4.
+
+Two findings from this campaign (both fixed in-tree):
+
+- **F-cache (scrub must write back).** First patched runs still showed
+  REMANENT: D-cache is write-back, so zeros issued immediately before reset
+  lingered in cache and never landed in PSRAM. Fix: `Cache_WriteBack_Addr`
+  (ROM, safe with interrupts off) over the window + fence before resetting,
+  in both the shutdown handler and the noos wrapper. Same flush added to
+  `plant` so the inspector never observes a cache artifact.
+- **F-memtest (loader must skip PSRAM memtest).** IDF's `SPIRAM_MEMTEST`
+  writes `p^0xAAAAAAAA` every 32 B across PSRAM without restoring, erasing
+  32/256 canary words on every loader boot before the inspector runs
+  (identified by residue `first_word=0xAABAAAAA` = `0x100000^0xAAAAAAAA` at
+  the 4 MB offset). Fix: `CONFIG_SPIRAM_MEMTEST=n` in `sdkconfig.defaults`
+  (reversible build flag; also ~1 s faster boot). Requires deleting the
+  stale generated `sdkconfig` once — `idf.py build` alone does not
+  re-apply changed defaults.
+
+Caveats: the `cycles`/`fired` RTC telemetry words (+4/+8 next to the magic)
+are not stable across boot (LP-RAM reuse by startup; observed garbage), so
+scrub duration is bounded analytically instead — 256 volatile writes + two
+1 KB ROM write-backs ≈ tens of µs at 360 MHz, ≪ 200 ms budget. The 1-word
+RTC magic itself gated correctly 6/6 runs; the production MicroPython port
+should scrub unconditionally (no flag needed). Tooling note: `sd_upload.py`
+VERIFY of the old 4.5 MB bundle failed `IO_ERROR`, blocking overwrite —
+worked around with `remove` first, then `upload` (small files fine).
+
+### G3 silicon observations
+
+`verify jitter_ms=` logged 1/3/4/5 across boots (bounded 1–5 ms, every boot,
+no oracle). `riscv32-esp-elf-objdump -d` confirms the compiler kept both
+loads in `secure_check_double` and the double `jal` per gate in `app_main`.
+Normal boot unaffected (multisig PASSED every run; anti-phishing words
+`ritual one enlist weasel` stable across all reboots). Double-branch cost is
+below the 1 ms log-timestamp resolution; cold loader time ~2.9 s (193 KB SD
+load + secp256k1 + 6 MB SHA-256 dominate).
